      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Initial on-site consultation and quote was within a few days of my Solarquotes enquiry. I waited for the other two companies to quote - one didn't come on-site but quoted remotely, but they were too expensive and only had a remote chance. The third didn't contact me for many days, but I was already happy with Ilumelec's customer service and quote, so I told them not to hurry. There were a few delays with installation because panels were in short supply due to that virus thing. The team arrived at 7:30am and were gone by 2:30pm. They left behind twenty panels, an inverter, and a bit of wire. But is was all working, and generating 4kW - nice job! (Ok, they don't normally have four guys working on one job - I was lucky). Complaints... not many - the local mains supply does rise at times which causes the inverter to shutdown for self protection. There are quite a few local solar installations all of which contribute to this potential problem. Apparantly the electricity distributor can adjust the local voltage if the frequency increases. I am still waiting for our retailer to flick their switch so we can start earning credits on our excess generation, but they may well blame the virus for an outbreak of delays. I also found 2 pieces of wire insulation 2cm long on the floor in a corner that they missed in the clean-up.",
